            {
              "id": "glog-941a5544-6951-4da7-9be9-23e3cd0534bf",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability in question is related to the `malloc` function in C++. `malloc` is a function that dynamically allocates memory at runtime. The problem arises when the size of the memory to be allocated is not properly validated or is influenced by an attacker, leading to a buffer overflow vulnerability. This can lead to various security issues such as code execution, denial of service, or information disclosure.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, `malloc(sizeof(hipDoubleComplex))`, the size of the memory to be allocated is determined by the size of `hipDoubleComplex`. If the size of `hipDoubleComplex` is not properly controlled or validated, it can lead to the aforementioned security issues.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always validate the size of the memory to be allocated. Never trust user input for determining the size. Also, consider using functions that limit the amount of memory that can be written, such as `calloc`, instead of `malloc`.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of using `malloc`, consider using `calloc` which initializes the allocated memory to zero. This can prevent uninitialized memory from being used in case of an error. Here is how you can do it:\n\n```cpp\nhipDoubleComplex* complex = (hipDoubleComplex*) calloc(1, sizeof(hipDoubleComplex));\nif (complex == NULL) {\n    // handle error\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `stdlib.h` library for the `malloc` function and `hip/hip_complex.h` for `hipDoubleComplex`.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP C++ Secure Coding](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n## CWE\n\nThis vulnerability can be classified under [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic' Buffer Overflow)](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS161085"
                ]
              }
